/*
:name: writer_bad_char
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: s\m
:pyrope_top: s\m
*/
//
// FIXED 2026-07-29 -- prp_writer now ESCAPES module names.
// Signal names went through the writer's backtick escaper; module names did not.
// A Verilog escaped identifier (`\s\m`) was emitted verbatim into the Pyrope
// module header, and `\` is not a legal Pyrope token, so the generated file could
// not even be TOKENIZED ("unexpected character in input").  quote_module_path()
// now backtick-quotes any `.`-component of a module name that is not a plain
// Pyrope identifier, at all three places a module name reaches the text: this
// header, the file-scope `const <name> = import(…)` binding, and the
// `<name>::[name=<inst>](…)` call site.  A normal name is byte-identical to
// before (the predicate accepts `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_$]*` minus the reserved
// words), so only escaped-id modules change.
//
// The emitted file is still named `s\m.prp` (the module name verbatim) -- that
// is what `:verilog_top:` resolves and what both harnesses open, so it stays.
pub comb `s\m`::[timecheck=false](a:u2) -> (o:u2) {
  o = (~a)#[0..=1]
}
